Xref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18395547\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000910 \"A mature T cell that differentiated and acquired cytotoxic function with the phenotype perforin-positive and granzyme-B positive.\")\n\n  Line 12132: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11685222\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000915 \"An alpha-beta intraepithelial T cell with the phenotype CD8-alpha-alpha-positive located in the columnar epithelium of the gastrointestinal tract. These cells have a memory phenotype of CD2-negative and CD5-negative.\")\n\n  Line 12404: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11685222\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000935 \"A CD4-negative, CD8-negative, alpha-beta intraepithelial T cell that is found in the columnar epithelium of the gastrointestinal tract.\")\n\n  Line 14663: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0412046911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36138472\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:8540632\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002063 \"A pulmonary alveolar epithelial cell that modulates the fluid surrounding the alveolar epithelium by secreting and recycling surfactants via specialized organelles called alveolar lamellar bodies. This cell type also contributes to tissue repair and can differentiate after injury into a pulmonary alveolar type 1 cell. This cuboidal cell is thicker than squamous alveolar cells, has a rounded apical surface that projects above the level of the surrounding epithelium, and its free surface is covered by short microvilli.\")\n\n  Line 14710: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0412046911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002066 \"A neuroendocrine cell found in the epithelium of the lungs and respiratory tract. This cell type is rounded or elliptical in shape, situated mainly in the basal part of the epithelium; regulates bronchial secretion, smooth muscle contraction, lobular growth, ciliary activity and chemoreception. Cell has an electron-lucent cytoplasm, contains numerous dense-cored vesicles with a clear halo between the core and the limiting membrane.\")\n\n  Line 14745: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002069 \"Mostly cylindrical, resemble Type 1 in their contents and the presence of a kinocilium and stereocilium apically; much greater variation in size, some almost span the entire thickness of the sensory epithelium, while others are smaller than Type 1; receive multiple efferent nerve boutons around their bases as well as afferent endings, which are small expansions rather than chalices.\")\n\n  Line 14767: # Class: obo:CL_0002071 (enterocyte of epithelium of large intestine)\n\n  Line 14769: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22288583\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35626748\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38872928\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002071 \"A columnar absorptive epithelial cell found in the epithelium of large intestine, specialized for water and electrolyte absorption. Unlike small intestinal enterocytes, those in the large intestine have fewer apical microvilli.\")\n\n  Line 14778: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002071 \"enterocyte of epithelium of large intestine\")\n\n  Line 14817: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15817800\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30291131\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37925434\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002075 \"A rare type of columnar epithelial cell that is part of the tracheobronchial epithelium. This cell is characterized by a distinctive tuft of apical microvilli, which extends into the cytoplasm, and a pear-shaped morphology, broad at the base and tapering to a narrow apex. It plays vital roles in chemosensation, producing cytokines like IL-25, and enhancing mucociliary clearance through acetylcholine release to support mucus movement and airway defense.\")\n\n  Line 15824: # Class: obo:CL_0002169 (basal cell of olfactory epithelium)\n\n  Line 15826: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7143026\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002169 \"An epithelial cell located on the basal lamina of the olfactory epithelium.\")\n\n  Line 15831: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002169 \"basal cell of olfactory epithelium\")\n\n  Line 15846: # Class: obo:CL_0002171 (globose cell of olfactory epithelium)\n\n  Line 15848: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17468753\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002171 \"A rounded or elliptical epithelial cell, with pale-staining open face nucleus and pale cytoplasm rich in free ribosomes and clusters of centrioles; form a distinct basal zone spaced slightly from the basal surface of the epithelium.\")\n\n  Line 15852: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002171 \"blastema cell of olfactory epithelium\")\n\n  Line 15853: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002171 \"globose cell of olfactory epithelium\")\n\n  Line 15995: # Class: obo:CL_0002184 (basal proper cell of olfactory epithelium)\n\n  Line 15997: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11891623\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002184 \"A flat or angular epithelial cell with condensed nuclei and darkly staining cytoplasm containing numerous intermediate filaments inserted into desmosomes contacting surrounding supporting cells; lie in contact with the basal lamina of olfactory epithelium.\")\n\n  Line 16002: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002184 \"basal proper cell of olfactory epithelium\")\n\n  Line 16196: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35271673\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002203 \"A tuft cell that is part of the epithelium of large intestine.\")\n\n  Line 16200: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002203 \"brush cell of epithelium proper of large intestine\")\n\n  Line 16202: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002203 \"tuft cell of epithelium of large intestine\")\n\n  Line 16223: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002205 \"A brush cell found in the epithelium of lobular bronchiole.\")\n\n  Line 16232: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002206 \"A brush cell of the epithelium in the terminal bronchiole.\")\n\n  Line 16241: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002207 \"Brush cell of the epithelium in the trachea.\")\n\n  Line 16252: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002208 \"A brush cell found in the epithelium of bronchus.\")\n\n  Line 16423: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002223 \"A cell of the transparent layer of simple cuboidal epithelium over the anterior surface of the lens; transform into lens fiber(s).\")\n\n  Line 16433: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lens_%28anatomy%29#Lens_epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002224 \"A cell of the cuboidal epithelium that covers the lens. The cells of the lens epithelium regulate most of the homeostatic functions of the lens. As ions, nutrients, and liquid enter the lens from the aqueous humor, Na+/K+ ATPase pumps in the lens epithelial cells pump ions out of the lens to maintain appropriate lens osmolarity and volume, with equatorially positioned lens epithelium cells contributing most to this current. The activity of the Na+/K+ ATPases keeps water and current flowing through the lens from the poles and exiting through the equatorial regions. The cells of the lens epithelium also serve as the progenitors for new lens fibers. It constantly lays down fibers in the embryo, fetus, infant, and adult, and continues to lay down fibers for lifelong growth.\")\n\n  Line 16536: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002234 \"A cell of the basal layer of the epithelium in the prostatic acinus.\")\n\n  Line 16546: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002235 \"A cell of the luminal layer of the epithelium in the prostatic acinus.\")\n\n  Line 16555: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15226377\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002236 \"A cell that constitutes the basal layer of epithelium in the prostatic duct.\")\n\n  Line 16564: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002237 \"A cell that constitutes the luminal layer of epithelium of prostatic duct.\")\n\n  Line 16709: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002250 \"A stem cell located in epithelium the based of the crypt of Lieberkuhn. Division of these cells serve both to maintain the stem cell population and produce the transit amplifying cells that are all precursors of all cell types that populate the intestinal epithelium.\")\n\n  Line 16801: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31869123\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002258 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the thyroid follicle epithelium, with a shape that ranges from squamous when inactive to cuboidal or columnar when active, reflecting its hormonal activity. Its apical surface is lined with microvilli projecting into the colloid-filled lumen, where it synthesizes, stores, and secretes the thyroid hormones thyroxine (T4) and triiodothyronine (T3), releasing them into the bloodstream in response to thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH).\")\n\n  Line 17140: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002288 \"A cell type that forms the boundary with the surrounding epithelium.\")\n\n  Line 17316: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15106942\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002303 \"A cell that is part of pigmented ciliary epithelium. This cell type uptakes sodium and chloride ions from stromal interstitium and passes the ions to non-pigmented ciliary epithelial cells via gap junctions.\")\n\n  Line 17328: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15106942\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002304 \"A cell that is part of non-pigmented ciliary epithelium. This cell type participates in aqueous humor formation by releasing solute, principally sodium and chloride ions received from pigmented epithelial cells via gap junctions, into the aqueous humor of the eye.\")\n\n  Line 17454: # Class: obo:CL_0002314 (external supporting cell of vestibular epithelium)\n\n  Line 17456: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20837532\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002314 \"An auditory epithelial support cell located in the vestibular epithelium that has many hallmarks of glial cells. This cell type express glial markers such as vimentin, S100, glutamate-aspartate transporter, low affinity neurotrophin receptor p75, glial fibrillary acidic protein, and proteolipid protein.\")\n\n  Line 17460: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002314 \"external supporting cell of vestibular epithelium\")\n\n  Line 17472: # Class: obo:CL_0002316 (supporting cell of vestibular epithelium)\n\n  Line 17474: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20837532\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002316 \"A supporting cell of the vestibular epithelium.\")\n\n  Line 17478: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002316 \"supporting cell of vestibular epithelium\")\n\n  Line 17481: # Class: obo:CL_0002317 (external limiting cell of vestibular epithelium)\n\n  Line 17483: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002317 \"An external limiting cell found in the vestibular epithelium.\")\n\n  Line 17487: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002317 \"external limiting cell of vestibular epithelium\")\n\n  Line 17643: # Class: obo:CL_0002330 (undifferentiated cell of bronchus epithelium)\n\n  Line 17645: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18757316\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002330 \"An undifferentiated columnar cell of the bronchus epithelium\")\n\n  Line 17648: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002330 \"undifferentiated cell of bronchus epithelium\")\n\n  Line 17659: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18757316\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002332 \"A multi-ciliated epithelial cell located in the bronchus epithelium, characterized by a columnar shape and motile cilia on its apical surface.\")\n\n  Line 17702: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15339667\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20568222\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9520465\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002337 \"A stem cell found in the basal layer of the epidermis, hair follicle, and sebaceous gland, characterised by its quiescent nature, high proliferative potential, and capacity for long-term self-renewal. This cell maintains epidermal homeostasis by producing transit-amplifying cells that differentiate to replenish the stratified squamous epithelium.\")\n\n  Line 17724: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15226377\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002339 \"A prostate epithelial cell that is CD133-positive, CD44-positive, integrin A2beta3-high. This cell is a stem cell for the prostate epithelium.\")\n\n  Line 17733: # Class: obo:CL_0002340 (luminal cell of prostate epithelium)\n\n  Line 17738: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002340 \"luminal cell of prostate epithelium\")\n\n  Line 17741: # Class: obo:CL_0002341 (basal cell of prostate epithelium)\n\n  Line 17743: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2673349\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002341 \"An undifferentiated cell of the prostate epithelium that lacks secretory activity.\")\n\n  Line 17746: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002341 \"basal cell of prostate epithelium\")\n\n  Line 18017: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002368 \"An epithelial cell of the respiratory tract epithelium.  These cells have an endoderm