{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778975982778,"sessionID":"ses_1ccc67d37ffefLbnlkOGwKYW9H","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_pKWZaxt9ngv1PfAKcrfFTFV9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"WIKIPEDIA:|Wikipedia:Intraepithelial","path":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","include":"cl-edit.owl"},"output":"Found 6 matches\n/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl:\n  Line 9440: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0815332181\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21860392\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32097634\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WIKIPEDIA:Spinous_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000649 \"A keratinocyte found within the stratum spinosum (prickle cell layer) of the epidermis, distinguished by numerous intercellular desmosomes, which give it a “prickly” or spiny appearance. Positioned above the mitotically active basal layer and beneath the granular layer, it contributes to the skin’s mechanical strength and barrier function, preventing water loss and pathogen entry. This cell expresses differentiation-specific keratins K1 and K10 in mice, unlike basal cells that express K5 and K14, and lacks the keratohyalin granules found in granular cells, marking its intermediate stage of epidermal differentiation.\")\n\n  Line 9442: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WIKIPEDIA:Spinous_cell\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000649 \"prickle cell of epidermis\")\n\n  Line 16020: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16824012\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32187560\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WIKIPEDIA:Basal_cell\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1073/pnas.1734203100\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002187 \"A mitotically active, columnar-shaped keratinocyte located in the stratum basale of the epidermis and attached to the basement membrane. This cell exhibits heterogeneity, encompassing stem and progenitor subpopulations with distinct molecular and proliferative characteristics (Haensel et al., 2020), and serves as the primary source of new keratinocytes for epidermal renewal, homeostasis, and regeneration.\")\n\n  Line 16046: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:1416031855\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29262154\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30355494\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30725734\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32843640\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WIKIPEDIA:Stratum_granulosum\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002189 \"A keratinocyte located in the stratum granulosum of the epidermis, characterized by the presence of keratohyalin granules containing filaggrin—which aggregate keratin filament —and by lamellar granules that secrete lipids and enzymes essential for forming the skin’s waterproof barrier. As these cells progress toward the surface, they adopt a flattened morphology and initiate keratinization to become corneocyte and form the protective stratum corneum. In human epidermis, granular keratinocytes are transcriptomically distinguished by high expression of differentiation markers such as DSC1, KRT2, IVL, and TGM3 (Wang et al., 2020), and LOR, FLG, and SPINK5 (Cheng et al., 2018).\")\n\n  Line 19302: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MP:0008894\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29674648\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Intraepithelial_lymphocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002496 \"A mature T cell that is located in an epithelium and is capable of a mucosal immune response.\")\n\n  Line 19317: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29674648\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Intraepithelial_lymphocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_9900000 \"A mature T cell that is located in the intestinal epithelium and is capable of a mucosal immune response.\")\n","metadata":{"matches":6,"truncated":false},"title":"WIKIPEDIA:|Wikipedia:Intraepithelial","time":{"start":1778975982753,"end":1778975982776}},"id":"prt_e333b4499001EmS3ZnoviFdIk6","sessionID":"ses_1ccc67d37ffefLbnlkOGwKYW9H","messageID":"msg_e333b2ad50013OX1DH7C9cbLzy"}}
